{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following MS C++ code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original MS C++ code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#define use_crt_defines\n#define _ert_No_deprecate\n\n#include <iostream>\n#include <cstdio>\n#include <cstring>\n#include <string>\n#include <algorithm>\n#include <cmath>\nusing namespace std;\n\nlong long n, x, y;\n\nlong long GCD(long long a, long long b) {\n    while (b) {\n        long long temp = b;\n        b = a % b;\n        a = temp;\n    }\n    return a;\n}\n\nclass Rational {\npublic:\n    long long num, den;\n    \n    Rational() : num(0), den(1) {}\n    Rational(long long n, long long d) : num(n), den(d) {}\n    \n    void operator-=(const Rational& other) {\n        num = num * other.den - other.num * den;\n        den = den * other.den;\n    }\n    \n    bool operator<(const Rational& other) const {\n        return num * other.den < other.num * den;\n    }\n    \n    void normalize() {\n        long long g = GCD(abs(num), abs(den));\n        if (g != 0) {\n            num /= g;\n            den /= g;\n        }\n        if (den < 0) {\n            num = -num;\n            den = -den;\n        }\n    }\n    \n    void show() const {\n        cout << num << \"/\" << den;\n    }\n};\n\nint main() {\n    cin >> x >> y >> n;\n    \n    Rational target(x, y);\n    Rational minDiff(50, 1);\n    Rational bestRational;\n    \n    for (long long i = 1; i <= n; ++i) {\n        long long q = (target.num * i) / target.den;\n        long long r = (target.num * i) % target.den;\n        \n        if (r > target.den / 2) {\n            q++;\n            r = target.den - r;\n        }\n        \n        Rational diff(r, i * target.den);\n        diff.normalize();\n        \n        if (diff < minDiff) {\n            minDiff = diff;\n            bestRational.num = q;\n            bestRational.den = i;\n        }\n    }\n    \n    bestRational.show();\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport math\n\ndef gcd(a, b):\n    while b:\n        a, b = b, a % b\n    return a\n\nclass Rational:\n    def __init__(self, n, d=1):\n        self.num = n\n        self.den = d\n        self.normalize()\n    \n    def __isub__(self, other):\n        self.num = self.num * other.den - other.num * self.den\n        self.den = self.den * other.den\n        self.normalize()\n        return self\n    \n    def __lt__(self, other):\n        return self.num * other.den < other.num * self.den\n    \n    def normalize(self):\n        g = gcd(abs(self.num), abs(self.den))\n        if g != 0:\n            self.num //= g\n            self.den //= g\n        if self.den < 0:\n            self.num = -self.num\n            self.den = -self.den\n    \n    def show(self):\n        print(f\"{self.num}/{self.den}\")\n\ndef main():\n    x, y, n = map(int, input().split())\n    \n    target = Rational(x, y)\n    minDiff = Rational(50, 1)\n    bestRational = Rational(0, 1)\n    \n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        q = (target.num * i) // target.den\n        r = (target.num * i) % target.den\n        \n        if r > target.den / 2:\n            q += 1